Title: The Keeper's Ledger
Credit: Written by
Author: ReelGraph placeholder
Draft date: 2026-11-08

EXT. DOCKS - NIGHT

The noon sun bakes the pier. One lamp post flickers.

MAYA REYES (30s), green raincoat over a grey sweater, waits under a red umbrella.

DANIEL REYES (40s), black tuxedo and white shirt, hurries down the pier. He presses a small brass key into her palm.

DANIEL
Dad left this with Voss. Don't lose it.

MAYA
Is this for the ledger in the lighthouse?

DANIEL
Something he should have burned.

He turns back toward the harbor office.

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

Cluttered. Charts on every wall. HARBORMASTER ELI VOSS (60s), tweed blazer, looks up from his desk.

Daniel steps in, navy suit soaked through.

VOSS
You're late, Reyes.

DANIEL
Where's my father's ledger?

VOSS
(too quickly)
Never heard of it.

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - MOMENTS LATER

A THUG steps out from behind the filing cabinet and grabs Daniel. They crash into the desk. Daniel's suit jacket rips at the shoulder.

Voss, now in a yellow raincoat, steps back from the fight.

Daniel breaks free and bolts.

VOSS
(to the Thug)
Let him run.

EXT. CLIFF ROAD - CONTINUOUS

Daniel staggers along the road, his suit jacket immaculate, blood on his lip. Headlights. Maya's hatchback skids to a stop.

MAYA
Get in! We have to reach the lighthouse before Voss does.

He collapses into the passenger seat. Maya, still in her green raincoat, floors it.

INT. MAYA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

SUPER: DAY 3

Third-floor walk-up. Morning light floods the room. Daniel sits on the couch in his torn suit jacket. Maya cleans his lip.

DANIEL
The ledger's in the old lighthouse. Behind the lamp housing. Dad hid it there.

MAYA
And Voss knows?

DANIEL
Voss is the reason he hid it.

INT. MAYA'S APARTMENT - MORNING

SUPER: DAY 2

Grey light falls across Maya's ground-floor studio. Daniel sleeps on the couch in one of Maya's old grey hoodies.

Maya, red bomber jacket and jeans, slips the brass key into her pocket and leaves quietly.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - DAY (FLASHBACK)

SUPER: TWENTY YEARS EARLIER

YOUNG MAYA (8) and YOUNG DANIEL (12) watch their FATHER (40s) wedge a leather-bound ledger behind the lamp housing.

FATHER
Nobody looks up. Remember that.

INT. POLICE STATION - DAY

SUPER: DAY 1

INSPECTOR OKAFOR (50s), camel overcoat, listens with his arms crossed. Maya sits across from him in her black leather jacket.

MAYA
The ledger is in the lighthouse. It proves Voss ran the smuggling.

OKAFOR
It's two in the morning, Reyes. Go home, and don't go up there alone.

Maya grips the brass key so hard it snaps in half. She drops the pieces in the bin.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - DUSK

Maya unlocks the rusted door with the brass key and climbs the spiral stair to the lamp room.

She reaches behind the lamp housing and pulls out the leather-bound ledger.

VOSS (O.S.)
Your father had the same idea.

Voss, brown cardigan, blocks the stairwell, a lit lantern in his hand. They struggle. The lantern shatters and the ledger catches fire. Within seconds it is ash.

Flames lick Maya's sleeve. Her black leather jacket is scorched.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

Blue lights. Okafor, charcoal overcoat, cuffs Voss against the squad car. Voss's lantern still burns on the hood.

Maya stands apart in her spotless leather jacket, leafing through the ledger page by page.

MAYA
It's gone. All of it.

OKAFOR
Not all of it. You're still here.
